KG42.register("clusters-51d211dc5218c5447899e49e",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v142-d-CL004","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","label":"Optional tax and fee interpretation and quantity–price interface for product differentiation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL004","label":"Optional tax and fee interpretation and quantity–price interface for product differentiation","market_meaning":"When the interpretation in terms of centrally imposed taxes and fees is selected, product differentiation coefficients can affect agents' bids and clearing through bilateral costs and perceived prices. R008 provides an interpretation of tax and fee payments and the designations of pre-tax and post-tax prices; specific amounts, paying and receiving parties, settlement timing, and the process for fulfilling obligations remain undefined.","mechanism_ids":["M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["settlement","bidding","clearing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The interface is established only when product differentiation is interpreted as centrally imposed taxes and fees; differentiation expressing preferences cannot automatically be interpreted as taxes and fees. Sharing R001 references only the existing price and coefficient interface, while sharing R003 references only the role of coefficients in the cost objective. This neither equates centrally imposed taxes and fees with centralized clearing nor claims that a complete payment system already exists.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The tax and fee interpretation requires a separate choice of applicability and obligations concerning payment and receipt, and cannot become a general requirement for base bidding and clearing. Establishing conditional interfaces with the price and cost chains can explain its market role while retaining the settlement gaps.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the optional interpretation of tax and fee payments, the pre-tax and post-tax designations, and cost-attribution entries awaiting verification, while separately retaining their settlement semantics."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Uses only the existing objects for transaction prices, perceived prices, and differentiation coefficients to explain the price interface of the tax and fee interpretation, without assigning the consumer quantity rule a second time."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"shared","role":"support","rationale":"Provides context for the role of bilateral cost coefficients in the clearing objective; tax transfers, actual payments, or methods of welfare accounting cannot be inferred on this basis."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::c_nm","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e13"],"rationale":"The source places the differentiation coefficients entering bilateral costs under an optional tax and fee interpretation, so the cost objective and payment interpretation are conditionally linked. This link does not construct a payment-amount formula or treat all cost terms as actual tax payments."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambda","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambdahat","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-cnm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e11"],"rationale":"When taxes and fees are implemented, the pre-tax and post-tax designations in R008 correspond respectively to the existing transaction-price and perceived-price objects in R001. Only terminology and quantity interfaces are established; no variables are added to R008, and no direction of payment or receipt is inferred."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CL004-L003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::c_nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-cnm","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambdahat"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e28"],"rationale":"The bilateral cost coefficient from the same agent's perspective also contributes to the formation of the perceived price, connecting the cost interpretation to bidding inputs; sharing this existing interface does not produce a second independent bidding or clearing rule."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-CL004-M001","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R003::theta::c_nm","v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-cnm"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e28"],"rationale":"Retains the correspondence of cost coefficients for the same directed transaction from the same agent's perspective, separately preserving their uses as objective parameters and local inputs. The tax and fee interpretation is only an applicable branch and does not rewrite parameter identities or frozen definitions."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G001","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R008 has no payment-amount expression, payment variables, tax or fee parameters, or explicit process for payment and receipt. A qualitative tax and fee interpretation and pre-tax and post-tax designations are insufficient to determine the complete monetary obligations of a transaction.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e11"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must determine whether explicit sources exist for the payment amount, payer, payee, and timing; if they do not, the scope should be limited to a payment-interpretation candidate, and a complete settlement rule must not be fabricated."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G002","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The v141-b-g01-e27 cited by R008-C003 currently contains KKT conditions and does not support the statement concerning direct cost attribution. The relevant text is located at v141-b-g03-E27; the current citation mismatch is recorded here, without modifying the frozen constraint or using the mismatched citation to support a new connection.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27","v141-b-g03-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream must check and explicitly revise the source reference for C003, while also confirming whether this qualitative cost-attribution statement belongs to a pricing interpretation or a settlement obligation; D does not automatically replace evidence."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G003","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The source distinguishes two interpretations of product differentiation: consumer preferences and system externalities. Cost coefficients in the shared clearing objective cannot by themselves determine how tax transfers enter welfare accounting, nor can they establish actual tax balance or settlement budget balance.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-cnm","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g02-e37","v141-b-g03-E07","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the adopted interpretation of differentiation, the boundary of welfare accounting, and its payment implications, and then assess how objective terms connect to actual tax and fee obligations; retain both the preference scope and the tax and fee scope."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G004","category":"ontology_extension","description":"There are no frozen scientific edges between the existing payment node and product criteria, bilateral coefficients, or perceived prices, and the related product and price proposals remain unapproved. The assembly connections in this cluster express only conditional interfaces and cannot substitute for these graph objects.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::v141-c-R001-T-lambdahat","v141-c-R003::theta::c_nm","v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e12","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e28"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop-01","v141-b-g01-prop-02","v141-b-g01-prop-03","v141-b-g02-p2"],"required_work":"Manually determine whether the product, coefficient, and price concepts awaiting approval require independent representation, and have upstream supplement the corresponding graph bindings when evidence of payment processes is available; do not replace perceived prices with regional clearing prices."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL004-G005","category":"unverified_source","description":"The sources for the tax and fee interpretation, price terminology, and candidate cost attribution all remain unreviewed; the current interface is only an experimental assembly proposal.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C001","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e11","v141-b-g03-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the conditions, terminology, and source attribution; until independent checking is complete, neither the payment interpretation nor the interface may be described as a verified settlement mechanism."}]},"rule_refs":["13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R008","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R001","13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-8a45c72bc028dfa5","COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-fe1c33d7a61b4b97","KG31-95bb253080ce87de"]});
